==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 40~80 seconds<sup>1,200f~2,400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Teacher Bun Bun]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Pigge]]s spawn, delay 46.67~66.67 seconds<sup>1,400f~2,000f</sup>.
**Infinite [[One Horn]]s spawn, delay 40~60 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,800f</sup>.
**1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This level requires some good strategy, particularly if you don't have any [[True Form]]s/[[Crazed Cats (origin)|Crazed Units]]. [[Delinquent Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Delinquent Cat]] and [[Bodhisattva Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bodhisattva Cat]]/[[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Monk Cat]] can be a great help, as they can help stall the movement of Teacher Bun Bun. More meatshields also help in this level when close to your base. Having three or more meatshields is vital to prevent Teacher Bun Bun from advancing, therefore units like [[Catburger (Special Cat)|Catburger]], [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Boogie Cat]] or [[Gold Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Gold Cat]] are useful if you have them.

At the beginning, spawn [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cats]] to stop Those Guys. Try to stall until you have level 8 Worker Cat and some money. Once you think you are ready, attack the base. [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] works well in this stage since it can kill the Those Guys that spawn at the beginning of the stage. This can allow you to stall for money quite effectively without spawning a single cat. Once you reach max, you can start by spawning meatshields and then ramp into more effective cats. Backliners like [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]] and [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]] are especially useful chipping away at Bun Bun from a safe distance. [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] is particularly useful if you happen to own them, since they can snipe Dark Emperor Nyandam and upcoming peons from a distance.

